<p>This is the current recorded model-backed execution of SupportFlow’s nine-turn scenario, with the clock frozen to <code>2027-07-15</code>. The interaction shows the stage boundaries and the approval prompt. The policy, refund arithmetic, ticket creation, and post-run durable-state assertions are explained and tested in the later lessons; model wording is not the policy authority.</p>

<h2 id="run-it-yourself">Run it yourself</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">cd pico-demo
npm run test:support-flow</code></pre>
<p>With <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> and <code>PICOFLOW_KEY</code>, the live scenario runs through one memory-backed session. Without live credentials, the deterministic policy tests still run and the live case is skipped.</p>

